WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.801
-Our first guest tonight
is a producer

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.937
and Emmy Award-winning actor
you know from shows such as

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:07.140
"This Is Us"
and "American Crime Story"

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.242
and films like "Waves"
and "Black Panther."

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:12.611
He just received his first
Academy Award nomination

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:14.914
for his role as Cliff
in "American Fiction,"

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.950
which is in theaters now.
Please welcome back to the show,

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:19.385
our friend, Sterling K. Brown,
everybody.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:21.387
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:30.797 align:start size:6% position:94% line:0%
♪♪

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:40.740 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:44.010
-I mean. I mean.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.579
Sterling!
-What's up, buddy?

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.781
-I have grown accustomed
to having you come on

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.818
and introducing you
as an Emmy Award-winning actor.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.352
-Sure.
-But Academy Award-nominated,

00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:54.286
it's a nice ring to it.

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:55.955
-It's not terrible.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:57.957
-It's not -- It's pretty good.
-I dig it, it's pretty cool.

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:59.359
-It's pretty good.
We were talking backstage.

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:00.626
-Yeah.
-It's very exciting.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.061
When you get nominated
for one of these awards,

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.162
there's a ton of events.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.030
-Yeah.
-Not just the press tour,

00:01:05.097 --> 00:01:06.832
but also, you get to hang out
with the other nominees,

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:08.868
and it's a pretty good bunch.
-This is very true.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.670
I got a chance to hang out --

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:13.472
She wasn't nominated this year
for an Academy Award,

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:15.074
but she was nominated
for an Emmy.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.475
Uh, Meryl Streep.
-Yes.

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:18.878
-We were at this --
Yeah, that's the right --

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:20.446
That's the right thing.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.681
Because if you know anything
about me, I'm a big Streep fan.

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:26.419
-Yeah.
-And she saw "American Fiction,"

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:28.688
and she told me how much
she enjoyed my work.

00:01:28.754 --> 00:01:30.055
And she kissed me.
-Yeah.

00:01:30.122 --> 00:01:32.391
-She kissed me, like,
right there.

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.260
And my wife saw it,
so it's legit, like,

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.162
it's not a thing.
-Yeah.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.630
-But it's also a thing.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:40.099
-Does it bother you at all?
Does it bother you at all,

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.834
knowing that
if she hadn't seen it

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.402
and was just lying to you,

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:46.005
you wouldn't be able to tell,
because she's so good?

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:47.807
-No. As long as
I wound up with the kiss,

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:49.442
that's all I really care about.
-The kiss was real.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:51.710
-That's it, that's it.
-Have you tried to get any

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:53.612
friends and family
to start referring to you

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:55.047
as
"the Academy Award-nominated?"

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:56.850
-Not just yet.
-Yeah.

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.117
-My son --

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.586
So I got nominated
for a few things before.

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.053
I got nominated
for a SAG Award,

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.522
what have you,
and my son loves to sort of

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:05.124
take the crap out of me, right?
-Yeah.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:06.492
-And he's like, what is this?
-Like, how old? What do we got?

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.094
-He's 12.
-Yeah. That's the take a crap.

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.161
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
He's like, what's that,

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:10.830
the Stupid Ass Gorilla award?

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:12.431
That's like SAG.
-Yep.

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:13.699
-Sort of thing.
-SAG,

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:15.234
you got to be honest,
I was asking for it.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.036
-There you go, there you go.
So I was like, yeah, whatever.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.371
So then I showed him,
I was like, hey,

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:20.874
you know, I got nominated
for an Oscar, you know?

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.776
And he goes, "Oh, yeah,
is that what? Uh..."

00:02:23.842 --> 00:02:26.412
-Yeah, too many letters.
-And then he was like...

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:29.649
Congrats, dad.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.715 --> 00:02:32.919
-There you go.
-It's cool, it's cool.

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:34.253
-You shared this
on social media.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.255
You had a real, you know --

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.224
At the end of the day,
yes, you're an actor,

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:41.360
but based on how you found
out, you are a dad first.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.129
And I found that very endearing

00:02:43.195 --> 00:02:45.131
because everybody always said,
how did you find out?

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:47.466
And the way you found out
is more in line with my life

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:48.834
as a dad than --
certainly my life --

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.903
-Because you have younger --
You're seven, five, two.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.739
I fell asleep
in the bedroom with him.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.007
I had my phone on.
The phone died.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:57.176
I woke up in the middle
of the night, got off the floor,

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:58.745
went to my bed with my wife,

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.513
which is where
I'm supposed to sleep.

00:03:00.579 --> 00:03:02.849
I charged my phone.
I wake up in the morning,

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:04.817
I go start feeding
them breakfast.

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:09.622
I go pick up the phone
that's now 126 text messages.

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:12.358
And I'm like, why am I -- 120 --
It's 7 in the morning!

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.259
Because I got nominated
for an Academy Award.

00:03:14.326 --> 00:03:15.961
-There you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:18.631
Now, based on that,

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.966
like, going into -- you know,
when you went to bed that night,

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.503
what was your --
what was your thinking?

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.971
I mean, obviously some people
had said this was possible.

00:03:26.038 --> 00:03:28.607
But...
-Some said it was possible.

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:31.577
I did not think it was.
-Okay.

00:03:31.643 --> 00:03:33.379
-I thought that there was
going to be other people

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.047
who were going to be nominated,
and I would have been more

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.750
than happy to congratulate them
and wish them well.

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:41.787
A young man from "The Holdovers"
and from "May/December"

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.188
and for other things.
Right?

00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:45.724
Uh, Willem Dafoe, etc...
So I was like, you know what?

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:47.259
If it happens, it happens.
If it doesn't, it doesn't.

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:49.595
I was not going to sweat it
one way or the other.

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.630
I was pleasantly surprised.

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:53.031
-It's a very nice thing
to be --

00:03:53.098 --> 00:03:56.435
-Seth, I still -- I feel like
a baby in this industry,

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.871
and when I see all the people
who I got nominated along with,

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:01.206
I'm just, like, honored
to be a part of the group.

00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:03.376
-It is a very nice thing,
and it's very well deserved.

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:04.677
You're wonderful in the film.

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:07.046
You're a wife is also an actor.
-She is.

00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:11.584
-And she's been nominated for
some things in the past as well.

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.152
And I was going to ask about

00:04:13.218 --> 00:04:14.987
who's your plus one
at the Academy Awards.

00:04:15.053 --> 00:04:17.323
I assumed it would be her.
-So this is -- Okay.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.958
My wife was the first person

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:22.494
ever nominated for something
in our couple.

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:25.331
She was a series regular
on "Boston Legal,"

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:26.899
and she got nominated
for best ensemble

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.600
for a Screen Actors
Guild Award.

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:32.171
Or, you know,
Stupid Ass Gorilla.

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:34.940
And I was like, oh man,
we get to go to the SAG Awards.

00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:36.309
It's going to be so much fun.
We get to it.

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:38.077
And she's like, "Actually,
Sterling,

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:40.379
like, I think I should
probably take my manager

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.415
because there's a good
networking opportunity for me."

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.851
And I was like, oh, cool,
cool, cool, I got it.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:48.354
No problem. That's fine.
Don't worry about it.

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:49.622
So then things ,like,
you know,

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:51.190
a few years later start
happening for your boy.

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.758
And she's like, "Oh, my God,
we get to go to the Emmys?"

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:55.327
And I was like,<i> we?</i>
I don't --

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:57.430
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:04.637
-This is a very, a very useful
lesson about a married couple.

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:06.739
And I should say,
you and your wife

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.574
obviously have
a nice perspective on this,

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.475
and you're also starting
a podcast together.

00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:11.911
-We are.

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:13.312
-And this is launching
on Valentine's Day.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.114
-Launching on Valentine's Day.
It's called

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:18.250
"We Don't Always Agree,
with Ryan and Sterling."

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:19.685
We've been married for 18 years.

00:05:19.751 --> 00:05:21.954
And you guys know, if you've
been together that long,

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:23.455
you don't always agree,

00:05:23.522 --> 00:05:24.857
but you figure a way
to make it out,

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.458
and it's --
we had so much fun.

00:05:26.525 --> 00:05:28.528
We're doing 12 episodes.
Hopefully, people

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:29.828
are enjoying them.
We'll do a season two.

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:31.464
-Now, I would ask, this --

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.467
is it -- when you talk to your
wife about how you don't agree.

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:35.835
-Yeah.
-I would imagine knowing

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:37.703
that other people
are going to hear it,

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.239
it makes it
the best versions of yourself.

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:41.206
Like if my wife --
-No.

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:42.775
-Oh, interesting.
-No.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:45.845
Well, what I want
is full accountability,

00:05:45.911 --> 00:05:49.081
because my wife will say crazy
things when we're by ourselves.

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:50.349
-Yes.
-I was like,

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:52.952
say that [bleep] right now.
-Yeah.

00:05:53.018 --> 00:05:54.854
-So that everybody
can hear it,

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.722
and then
we'll find out who's crazy.

00:05:56.788 --> 00:06:00.359
-I mean, when -- I couldn't
agree with you more.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:02.461
When my wife and I are fighting,
the amount I want to be like,

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:03.996
"You know what?
Let's do it as a podcast."

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:06.265
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:06:06.331 --> 00:06:07.533
-Let's take it
out in the streets.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:08.935
-Let's take it out
in the streets.

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:11.103
-Yeah, we'll get some sponsors.
-There you go.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.571
Um, I have a lot more
to ask you.

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:14.874
Will you stick around?
You guys, that's Sterling.

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:16.275
More after this.

